### On what date did Nigeria gain independence from British colonial rule?
Answer: Nigeria gained independence from British colonial rule on **October 1, 1960**.

Source URL: https://www.globalcitizen.org/en/content/facts-to-know-about-nigeria-independence/

### How many complete years had elapsed since Nigeria's independence as of October 1, 2020?
Answer: As of October 1, 2020, 60 complete years had elapsed since Nigeria's independence, as stated in President Buhari's speech referencing "our 60 years of existence as a nation."

Source URL: https://www.cnn.com/2015/03/25/africa/gallery/nigeria-moments-in-history/index.html

### What were the start and end dates of Nigeria's first period of military rule (the military government of Johnson Aguiyi-Ironsi and Yakubu Gowon from 1966 to 1975)?
Answer: The first period of military rule in Nigeria began in January 1966, when Maj-Gen Johnson Aguiyi-Ironsi formed a military government following a coup, and ended in July 1975, when General Yakubu Gowon was overthrown by Brigadier Murtala Ramat Mohammed.

Source URL: https://www.bbc.com/news/world-africa-13951696

